From 2c4127472b40e6ff2b65593843d8af16446ea5e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nex <63727521+LuCiLuna@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 04:40:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 084/110] HACK: soc: qcom: describe the OnePlus sensors to the
 SLPI

The OnePlus sensor drivers in the SLPI firmware only enable the sensors
the application processor lists in SMEM item 130 (chip per slot,
mounting direction, tuning). Downstream oplus_sensor_devinfo fills it
from an oplus,sensor-devinfo node; without it libssc finds no sensors.

Add the SMEM part of that driver (same struct layout), built in so the
item exists before the SLPI boots, and the downstream node for the 9
Pro. Also keep the SSC sensor rails (pm8350c L2/L7, downstream
qcom,msm-ssc-sensors vddio/vdd) on.

With hexagonrpcd serving the persist registry, the accelerometer,
ambient light, proximity and magnetometer report through libssc.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
